\\
801.41;+42216,;35~WP-start~16
NEWS Score: 0-2 Low: Continue to monitor per facility clinical 
algorithms.\\
\\NEWS Score: 3-4 Medium: Assess threat, confer with site-specific nursing
resources, assess if acute illness or unstable chronic disease, follow 
local clinical algorithms.\\
     Single parameter score of 3 in any one category should not drive\\ 
      change in VS frequency.\\
\\NEWS Score: 5-6 High: Your patient is at risk to deteriorate rapidly. 
Contact provider and site-specific nursing resources, follow local 
clinical algorithms.\\
     Increase VS every 2 hours x 3 (6 hours total); reassess NEWS with\\
      each VS set\\
 \\NEWS Score: = or > 7 Immediate Action: Call RRT, notify charge RN and
primary team immediately, follow local clinical algorithms.\\
     Notify site specific nursing resources and activate Rapid Response\\ 
      immediately. Continuous monitoring of VS is recommended.
